{"title":"Reading sectors under UEFI","slug":"Reading_sectors_under_UEFI","html":"<p>Note that you don't necessarily need to access raw block devices, because UEFI provides <a data-wiki=\"Loading files under UEFI\" href=\"#/library/Loading_files_under_UEFI\">files abstraction</a> with EFI_SIMPLE_FILE_SYSTEM_PROTOCOL (typically limited to <a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT\">FAT</a>-only partitions).</p>\n<h2 id=\"iterating_on_disks\">Iterating on Disks</h2>\n<p>If you already have a handle for a block device, then your job is easy. However more often you don't, which means first you must query the list of block devices in the system. Because you don't know in advance how many devices there are, you must locate the BLOCK_IO_PROTOCOL twice.</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb1-1\">EFI_GUID bioGuid <span class=\"op\">=</span> BLOCK_IO_PROTOCOL<span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-2\">EFI_BLOCK_IO <span class=\"op\">*</span>bio<span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-3\">EFI_HANDLE <span class=\"op\">*</span>handles <span class=\"op\">=</span> NULL<span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-4\">UINTN handle_size <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"dv\">0</span><span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><span class=\"co\">/* first, locate the protocol with empty buffer */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-7\">status <span class=\"op\">=</span> uefi_call_wrapper<span class=\"op\">(</span>BS<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>LocateHandle<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">5</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> ByProtocol<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span>bioGuid<span class=\"op\">,</span> NULL<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span>handle_size<span class=\"op\">,</span> handles<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><span class=\"cf\">if</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>status <span class=\"op\">!=</span> EFI_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL <span class=\"op\">||</span> handle_size <span class=\"op\">==</span> <span class=\"dv\">0</span><span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-9\">    <span class=\"co\">/* AUCH, error we don't have BLOCK_IO */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><span class=\"co\">/* get a buffer for the handles now that we know the buffer size */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-13\">status <span class=\"op\">=</span> uefi_call_wrapper<span class=\"op\">(</span>BS<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>AllocatePages<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">4</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">0</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">2</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>handle_size <span class=\"op\">+</span> PAGESIZE<span class=\"op\">-</span><span class=\"dv\">1</span><span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">/</span> PAGESIZE<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>EFI_PHYSICAL_ADDRESS<span class=\"op\">*)&amp;</span>handles<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><span class=\"cf\">if</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>EFI_ERROR<span class=\"op\">(</span>status<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">||</span> handles <span class=\"op\">==</span> NULL<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-15\">    <span class=\"co\">/* AUCH, error memory allocation failed */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><span class=\"co\">/* second round, locate the protocol with big enough buffer */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-19\">status <span class=\"op\">=</span> uefi_call_wrapper<span class=\"op\">(</span>BS<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>LocateHandle<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">5</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> ByProtocol<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span>bioGuid<span class=\"op\">,</span> NULL<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span>handle_size<span class=\"op\">,</span> handles<span class=\"op\">);</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Now \"handles\" is an array that has a handle for each and every block device in the system.</p>\n<p>We should iterate on that array, and use ith handle to get the block IO interface for a device.</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb2\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb2-1\"><span class=\"cf\">for</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>i <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"dv\">0</span><span class=\"op\">;</span> i <span class=\"op\">&lt;</span> handle_size <span class=\"op\">/</span> <span class=\"kw\">sizeof</span><span class=\"op\">(</span>EFI_HANDLE<span class=\"op\">);</span> i<span class=\"op\">++)</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-2\">    status <span class=\"op\">=</span> uefi_call_wrapper<span class=\"op\">(</span>BS<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>HandleProtocol<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">3</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> handles<span class=\"op\">[</span>i<span class=\"op\">],</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span>bioGuid<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">void</span> <span class=\"op\">**)</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span>bio<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-3\">    <span class=\"co\">/* if unsuccessful, skip and go over to the next device */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-4\">    <span class=\"cf\">if</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>EFI_ERROR<span class=\"op\">(</span>status<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">||</span> bio <span class=\"op\">==</span> NULL <span class=\"op\">||</span> bio<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>Media<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>BlockSize<span class=\"op\">==</span><span class=\"dv\">0</span><span class=\"op\">)</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-5\">        <span class=\"cf\">continue</span><span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-6\">    <span class=\"co\">/* </span><span class=\"al\">TODO</span><span class=\"co\">: do something with that device. */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-7\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"loading_raw_sectors\">Loading Raw Sectors</h2>\n<p>The \"bio\" interface inside the iteration above refers to one particular device. You can use that interface to load sectors from that device quite easily:</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb3\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb3-1\">UINT8 mbr<span class=\"op\">[</span><span class=\"dv\">512</span><span class=\"op\">];</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-2\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-3\">status <span class=\"op\">=</span> uefi_call_wrapper<span class=\"op\">(</span>bio<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>ReadBlocks<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">5</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> bio<span class=\"op\">,</span> bio<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>Media<span class=\"op\">-&gt;</span>MediaId<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">1</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">512</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span>mbr<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-4\"><span class=\"cf\">if</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>EFI_ERROR<span class=\"op\">(</span>status<span class=\"op\">))</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-5\">    <span class=\"co\">/* AUCH, error reading sector */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-6\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"see_also\">See also</h2>\n<h3 id=\"articles\">Articles</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a data-wiki=\"UEFI\" href=\"#/library/UEFI\">UEFI</a></li>\n<li><a data-wiki=\"UEFI App Bare Bones\" href=\"#/library/UEFI_App_Bare_Bones\">UEFI Bare Bones</a></li>\n<li><a data-wiki=\"EFI System Partition\" href=\"#/library/EFI_System_Partition\">EFI System Partition</a></li>\n<li><a data-wiki=\"Loading files under UEFI\" href=\"#/library/Loading_files_under_UEFI\">Loading files under UEFI</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"external_links\">External Links</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.uefi.org/specifications\" rel=\"noopener\">UEFI specifications et al.</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://sourceforge.net/p/gnu-efi/code/ci/master/tree/\" rel=\"noopener\">GNU-EFI source</a></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"iterating_on_disks","text":"Iterating on Disks","level":2},{"id":"loading_raw_sectors","text":"Loading Raw Sectors","level":2},{"id":"see_also","text":"See also","level":2},{"id":"articles","text":"Articles","level":3},{"id":"external_links","text":"External Links","level":2}],"categories":["UEFI","x86-64"],"rating":null,"flags":[],"words":460,"summary":"Note that you don't necessarily need to access raw block devices, because UEFI provides files abstraction with EFI_SIMPLE_FILE_SYSTEM_PROTOCOL (typically limited to FAT -only partitions).","updated":"2020-12-15","authors":["Bzt"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/Reading_sectors_under_UEFI","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=Reading_sectors_under_UEFI&action=history","backlinks":[{"t":"Loading files under UEFI","s":"Loading_files_under_UEFI"},{"t":"POSIX-UEFI","s":"POSIX_UEFI"}],"lessons":[{"id":"t15m2l3","title":"From UEFI to your kernel","kind":"further"}]}